# S01 — BAM with declared @RG satisfies a matching read-group consumer
#
# SUPPLEMENT — post-hoc descriptive acceptance control. NOT part of the
# pre-registered confirmatory analysis; authored after the primary outcome
# was seen; never enters the false-accept denominator.
# The producer declares BAM[sort_order=coordinate] with read_groups
# required=true and fields ID,SM,PL; the consumer declares the same named
# contract. The declared @RG metadata satisfies the consumer requirement,
# so no TYPE diagnostic. This supplies the primary corpus's missing
# TYPE-005 accept-side contrast (descriptive supplement only).
#
# EXPECTED (authored 2026-11-28 from the published contract, before the supplement run):
#   accept — no TYPE diagnostic.

[workflow]
name = "s01"

[types.bam_rg]
format = "bam"
sort_order = "coordinate"

[types.bam_rg.read_groups]
required = true
fields = ["ID", "SM", "PL"]

[[rules]]
name = "produce"
output = ["aln.bam"]
shell = "bwa mem ref.fa r1.fq r2.fq | samtools sort -o aln.bam"
[rules.types]
outputs = { default = "bam_rg" }

[[rules]]
name = "bqsr"
input = ["aln.bam"]
output = ["recal.table"]
shell = "gatk BaseRecalibrator -I aln.bam -R ref.fa -O recal.table"
[rules.types]
inputs = { default = "bam_rg" }
